Author: shirotech <van@shirotech.com>
Date:   Thu May 14 18:53:09 2026 +0000

    optimize: slurp-log-into-vec [KEPT] -10.4% to -11.0% on reopen_10k
    
    Replace the BufReader-based replay with a one-shot File::read_to_end
    into a Vec, then iterate length-prefixed slices in memory and let
    bincode::deserialize borrow them directly. Removes per-record memcpy
    into a separate payload buffer plus BufReader refill bookkeeping. The
    BufReader import is no longer used and is dropped from std::io.
    
    Three runs vs the fixed baseline: reopen_10k -10.96% / -10.97% /
    -10.43%; all other scenarios within +/-1.1% noise; no regressions
    past +0.43%. Verdict KEPT per /optimize gate.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

